<title>HONG KONG: Hong Kong-Melbourne '96 air freight falls 15.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Hong Kong-Melbourne '96 air freight falls 15.4 pct.</headline>
<byline>Jim Gilchrist</byline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>There was a 15.4 per cent fall in the amount of air freight carried between Hong Kong and Melbourne during 1996 compared to 1995, according to latest air transport statistics issued by Australia's Department of Transport and Regional Development.</p>
<p>Auckland-Sydney remained the major contributor for international freight carried by the top ten city pairs with 7.2 per cent of the total for 1996.</p>
<p>Auckland-Melbourne with a 42 per cent rise, Singapore-Perth 10.7 per cent and Brisbane-Auckland 8.4 per cent recorded the most significant increases during the year. Hong Kong-Melbourne recorded the biggest decrease followed by an 11 per cent fall in air freight between Los Angeles-Sydney.</p>
<p>Details of freight carried by route in 1996 in tonnes compared to 1995 on the top ten routes included:</p>
<p> Route		    Year ended   Year ended   Pct change</p>
<p> in tonnes		  Dec 96	 Dec 95     96 over 95</p>
<p> Auckland/Sydney	  42,210	 40,939     up    3.1</p>
<p> Sydney/Singapore	 36,249	 33,654     up    7.7</p>
<p> Hong Kong/Sydney	 35,808	 34,514     up    3.7</p>
<p> Auckland/ Melbourne    33,735	 23,764     up   42.0</p>
<p> Singapore/ Melbourne   29,296	 29,732     down  1.5</p>
<p> Los Angeles/ Sydney    28,239	 31,715     down 11.0</p>
<p> Hong Kong/Melbourne    23,068	 27,277     down 15.4</p>
<p> Tokyo/Sydney	     21,385	 21,970     down  2.7</p>
<p> Singapore/ Perth	 20,799	 18,796     up   10.7</p>
<p> Auckland/ Brisbane     12,597	 11,617     up    8.4</p>
<p> Other city pairs	299,495	276,919     up    8.2</p>
<p> ALL CITY PAIRS    582,883 550,900 5.8</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
